                <pb facs="0470" n="352" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg352"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00Detention/2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Ciudad Juarez</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dye</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">El
                                Paso, Tex</hi></placeName>., <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-03-08T15:30:00-07:00">March 8, 1929—3:30
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:54 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Agreed between commanders that General Ramos and his Federal troops cross into
                    United States and be interned. This to proceed at once. Fort Bliss military
                    police in charge of the plan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dye</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
